1662	3828	1655	5	**The perfect comedy**\r\n\r\nThe legendary Coen brothers deliver a hilarious and deeply unique odyssey that defies conventions and embraces the glorious absurdity of life. Through "The Dude" Lebowski, a Los Angeles slacker whose existence revolves around bowling and White Russians, we witness his peaceful routine upended when he is mistaken for a millionaire who shares his last name. What begins as a simple quest to recover his rug—ruined by a pair of thugs—swiftly unravels into an intricate web of kidnappings, deception, and nihilistic characters in true Coen fashion.\r\n\r\nThe film's greatest triumph lies in its characters, sculpted with surgical precision to perfectly fit the actors portraying them. The protagonist is Lebowski, the quintessential antihero: a laid-back pacifist who, despite the surrounding chaos, remains fiercely loyal to his passive philosophy. He is flanked by his best friend Walter (John Goodman), a volatile Vietnam veteran obsessed with the rules of a Jewish faith that is not originally his own.\r\n\r\nThe Coen brothers once again demonstrate their genius for world-building, seamlessly intertwining black comedy, surreal humor, and social satire. The direction is impeccable, featuring memorable dream sequences and an extraordinary narrative pacing that sweeps the viewer into a whirlwind of unpredictable events. Ultimately, "The Big Lebowski" is a meditation on identity, purpose, and the futility of expectations. "The Dude," in all his simplicity, stands as a paradigm of passive resistance against the complexity and madness of the modern world.	\N	\N	pending	2022-12-25 23:43:51+03	2026-09-22 19:53:47+03
