3343	4912	18	4	Clint Eastwood has assembled a really strong cast here for this daring look at just how taboos are dealt with, even now, in 21st century Boston. We begin with three lads messing about with some freshly laid concrete before a police car arrives and forces "Dave" to get in the back. Nobody hears from him for four days and thereafter he is completely silent about what went on and we advance into their adulthood. "Dave" (Tim Robbins) is married to "Celeste" (Marcia Gay Harden); "Sean" (Kevin Bacon) is a cop and "Jimmy" (Sean Penn) runs a store with wife "Annabeth" (Laura Linney). They don't have much to do with each other any more, but that's about to change when "Katie" - the teenage daughter of "Jimmy" is found slain. "Sean" is the lead detective on the case with his partner - the curiously named "Whitey" (Laurence Fishburne), and are quickly on the case. Unhappy with the pace of things, ex-con "Jimmy" asks a couple of his less scrupulous friends to look into just what happened. What adds to the confusion is that on the very night of her death, "Dave" returned home with a bad cut on his hand. He claims to have been mugged, but as this clearly troubled man becomes the subject of the investigation - official and unofficial, his story starts to wobble a bit, his wife begins to doubt the voracity of his story and the race is on for "Sean" to find the culprit before the bereft dad takes matters into his own hands. On the whodunnit front, there are red herrings galore to keep us guessing and at times I felt that Eastwood was deliberately misleading us with conflicting stories to keep the tension high but not at the expense of the humanity of these three men and the two wives. It's there that this film stands out with both Penn and Robbins at the top of their games and with the slightly ruthless Linney also presenting a character that appears sparingly, but potently. At times I thought there were annoying bits of the plot missing, but as the threads all knit together it rather effectively exposes the demons, flaws and anxieties of these men as they deal with grief, fear and revenge.	\N	\N	pending	2026-06-30 17:43:00+03	2026-06-30 17:45:40+03
