4419	13139	2286	5	Pixar cooked with this one! *Turning Red* is probably one of the studio's most chaotic features, but shockingly, that doesn't mean the movie is bad. From its wild anime-style visuals to its unhinged comedy, this movie delivers what we expect from the company, but with a little bit extra. The mother-daughter bond between Mei Lee and Ming Lee is very wholesome because you can see as far back as the opening these two are very close and are about to be even closer, even if Ming starts off as a control freak before we learn why she's so strict. I also really liked how the concept of family doesn't stop at biological family members, as Mei's friends-Miriam Mendelsohn, Abby Park, and Priya Mangal-are a found family of sorts: While Mei's parents Ming and Jin operate on a clash of forced perfection and silent acceptance, Mei's friends accept her as she is and don't try to change her to fit in. Even when she didn't have her panda, they still chose to be her friend because they all had the same interests and desires. Speaking of the red panda, it looks so cute and I love how it acts as a metaphor for untapped anger issues. This is especially important if you remember the *Inside Out* franchise, where Anger is represented with the color red as well. While I will admit it is kind of lazy the panda explodes in pink smoke to transform, especially after *Luca* showed the sea monsters gradually shapeshifting into humans on dry land, it is still a fun transformation. My real biggest criticism with this movie is how little of a role Jin had. I feel like if he was a bigger character he could be a great mediator in Mei and Ming's tension. Pixar only pushed him aside because the story is about the friction between Mei and Ming, and that feels like bad storytelling. At least, that's how I feel. The soundtrack is also very timely for the era they captured (early 2000s), and the songs the fictional boy band 4-Town performed are absolute banger hits. So overall, while *Turning Red* does have a lazy animation choice in making the red panda poof in a cloud of pink smoke and pushes Jin aside unnecessarily, I still think the movie's a great addition to the Pixar roster and I hope it gets a sequel.	\N	\N	pending	2026-09-23 01:19:47+03	2026-09-23 01:19:47+03
