se than "well I thought the sacrifice was worth it for the good of 'OUR' people". Why they had him say "my" is anyone's guess.\r\n7. Less stoic one-liners and less stoic "No! <*thrusts sword into ground*>" moments. We've seen it numerous times and it's just utterly boring and contrived at this point.	\N	\N	pending	2024-03-10 08:49:18+03	2024-03-19 19:40:46+03
